{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":371975,"duration_api_ms":368799,"ttft_ms":3607,"ttft_stream_ms":2840,"time_to_request_ms":101,"num_turns":52,"result":"## Investigation Report\n\n### Task Summary\nThe requester wants every connected WebSocket client to receive a small \"server is shutting down\" notice immediately before its connection is torn down, as an automatic part of the graceful-shutdown sequence the framework already runs on SIGTERM (via `enableShutdownHooks`/`NestApplicationContext.close()`), for both the socket.io and `ws` platform adapters, with zero behavioral change for gateways with no connected clients and for apps that never use WebSockets.\n\n### Candidate Cells\n| Cell | Reason | Priority |\n|---|---|---|\n| `packages/platform-ws/adapters/ws-adapter.ts` | `WsAdapter.close()` already enumerates `server.clients` right before terminating them | High |\n| `packages/platform-socket.io/adapters/io-adapter.ts` | `IoAdapter.close()` already wraps the server-close call; socket.io's `.emit()` broadcasts to all connected sockets | High |\n| `packages/websockets/constants.ts` / `internal.ts` | Shared event-name constant must be defined once and re-exported for both platform packages, matching existing pattern (`DISCONNECT_EVENT`, `CLOSE_EVENT`, etc.) | High |\n| `packages/websockets/adapters/ws-adapter.ts` (`AbstractWsAdapter`) | Confirmed generic base, no client-enumeration capability — verified no change needed | Informational |\n| `packages/core/nest-application.ts`, `nest-application-context.ts` | Confirmed shutdown sequence already routes here unconditionally — verified no change needed | Informational |\n| `packages/websockets/socket-module.ts` | Confirmed single call site of `adapter.close(server)` — verified no change needed | Informational |\n\n### Tracing Summary\n1. Kubernetes sends `SIGTERM` → `NestApplicationContext.listenToShutdownSignals`'s `cleanup(signal)` (nest-application-context.ts:362-394) runs: `prepareClose()` → `callDestroyHook()` → `callBeforeShutdownHook(signal)` → `dispose()` → `callShutdownHook(signal)`.\n2. `NestApplication.dispose()` (nest-application.ts:97-108) is the override actually invoked (since `app.close()`/shutdown hooks operate on a `NestApplication` instance): `await this.socketModule?.close();` runs first, before `microservicesModule.close()` and `httpAdapter.close()`.\n3. `SocketModule.close()` (socket-module.ts:128-145): early-returns if `!this.applicationConfig` or `!adapter` (true for apps with zero gateways registered, since `socketModule` itself is only lazily constructed in `loadSocketModule()` when `@nestjs/websockets` is present and a gateway triggers `connectGatewayToServer`). Otherwise it does `servers = this.socketsContainer.getAll()`, filters those with a live `server`, and calls `adapter.close(server)` for each, then `adapter.dispose()`, then `socketsContainer.clear()`. Grep confirms this is the **only** call site of `adapter.close(...)` in the repo.\n4. For `WsAdapter` (platform-ws/adapters/ws-adapter.ts:195-205): `close(server)` builds `closeEventSignal` around `server.close(cb)`, then `for (const ws of server.clients) ws.terminate()`, then awaits the close signal. `server.clients` is a `Set<WebSocket>` — empty when no clients connected, so the loop body never executes (safe by default).\n5. For `IoAdapter` (platform-socket.io/adapters/io-adapter.ts:95-101): `close(server)` — if `forceCloseConnections && server.httpServer === this.httpServer`, returns early without calling `super.close(server)` at all (because the shared HTTP server's own `close()`, invoked later by the HTTP adapter, will tear down those sockets). Otherwise calls `super.close(server)` → `AbstractWsAdapter.close()` → `server.close(resolve)`.\n6. Verified in `node_modules/socket.io/dist/namespace.js:311-312`: `Namespace.prototype.emit(ev, ...args)` literally returns `new BroadcastOperator(this.adapter).emit(ev, ...args)` — i.e. it does **not** behave like a local `EventEmitter.emit`; it broadcasts the event to every socket currently in the namespace via the adapter. `Server` extends `Namespace`, so the same holds for the root namespace. This confirms `server.emit(SHUTDOWN_EVENT, payload)` is the correct, idiomatic way to notify all connected socket.io clients before closing.\n7. Verified in `node_modules/ws/lib/websocket.js:455-481` and `sender.js`: `ws.send(data, cb)` invokes `cb` once the frame write completes (`cb(err)` fired from the sender's dispatch/write-callback chain), confirming the callback reliably sequences \"written to the OS socket buffer\" before any subsequent `terminate()` call — i.e., awaiting each client's `send` callback before calling `ws.terminate()` on that same client guarantees the notice is not dropped by the abrupt destroy.\n\n### Data Flow Analysis\nThe shutdown notice never crosses cell boundaries beyond what's already scoped: `SocketModule.close()` passes the raw server object straight through to `adapter.close(server)` unchanged; the new logic is entirely internal to each concrete adapter's own `close()` method, reading only the server object's existing client collection (`server.clients` for `ws`; the server/namespace's own broadcast surface for socket.io) — no new data enters or leaves `SocketModule`, `SocketsContainer`, or `packages/core`.\n\n### Manifest Algorithm Analysis\nNot applicable — `packages/websockets`, `packages/platform-ws`, and `packages/platform-socket.io` have no CODEMANIFEST cells yet (confirmed via `goga schema`, which lists only `packages/core/*`, `packages/common/exceptions`, `packages/platform-express/adapters`, `packages/platform-fastify/adapters`). No manifest algorithm governs this code today; the change is plain-code with no manifest reconciliation required for these three packages.\n\n### Affected Usages\n| Usage | Cell | Classification | Reason |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| N/A | N/A | N/A | No `.usages` files exist for the affected cells (none of the three packages are goga-cell-managed); no usage docs are directly or indirectly affected |\n\n### Rejected Hypotheses\n- **\"Modify `AbstractWsAdapter.close()` generically to notify+close.\"** Rejected: the base class's `TServer`/`TClient` generics guarantee only `on`/`close`, giving no cross-transport way to enumerate connected clients or their readiness state; forcing this up would require either an unsafe cast or a new abstract method that both subclasses must implement anyway — no simpler than overriding `close()` directly in each concrete adapter, and it would touch a class with two implementers, widening blast radius for no benefit.\n- **\"Change `ws.terminate()` to `ws.close()` for a graceful handshake instead of manual send+terminate.\"** Rejected: `server.close()` on a raw `ws.Server` only invokes its callback once every client connection has fully closed; relying on each client's graceful close handshake risks hanging the whole shutdown sequence indefinitely if a client never acknowledges (exactly why the current code already force-terminates). Keeping `terminate()` but sequencing a flushed `send()` first preserves the existing bounded-time guarantee while still delivering the notice.\n- **\"Add a configurable message/event-name option on `NestApplicationOptions`.\"** Rejected as out of requested scope — the request asks only for an automatic default notice, not a configuration surface; adding one would be speculative and violates \"minimize scope.\"\n- **\"Notify from `SocketModule.close()` instead of inside each adapter.\"** Rejected: `SocketModule` only has the raw `server` object with no transport-specific knowledge of how to enumerate/notify clients — that logic can only live where the code already knows the concrete client shape, i.e. inside each concrete adapter's `close()`.\n\n### Confirmed Root Cause\nThis is a net-new feature request, not a bug — there is no existing hook, dead code, or partial implementation for a shutdown notice anywhere in the three target packages. The correct insertion points are the two concrete adapters' existing `close(server)` overrides (`platform-ws/adapters/ws-adapter.ts:195-205` and `platform-socket.io/adapters/io-adapter.ts:95-101`), since both already run unconditionally, exactly once, at exactly the moment (immediately before client teardown) the request calls for, with zero new call sites needed anywhere in `packages/core` or `packages/websockets`.\n\n### Confidence Level\n**HIGH** — every claim was verified directly against source line numbers, the single confirmed call site of `adapter.close`, and the actual installed `socket.io`/`ws` library source (not documentation assumptions). No ambiguity remains about call ordering, emit-broadcast semantics, or send-callback flush guarantees.\n\n### Breaking Change Assessment\n1. **Will an existing function call with the same arguments produce different behavior?** NO — `close(server)`'s external signature and return type (`Promise<void>`/`Promise<any>`) are unchanged; for zero connected clients, the added code paths are no-ops (empty `Set`/no sockets in namespace), so behavior is byte-for-byte identical to today.\n2. **Will existing file paths change?** NO — no files are moved or renamed; one new test-only directory (`packages/platform-ws/test/`) is added, which is purely additive.\n3. **Will output format change?** NO — no public return value or REST/RPC contract changes; the only new \"output\" is an additional WebSocket frame/event sent to already-connected clients during shutdown, which is the explicit purpose of this task, not an accidental format change to any existing API.\n4. **Will return value semantics change?** NO — `close()` still resolves once the server (and, in the `ws` case, its clients) are closed; the only addition is that each client's socket now receives one extra frame first, awaited via its own flush callback, which still resolves before `terminate()`/`server.close()`'s callback fires.\n5. **Will manifest-defined guarantees be altered?** NO — not applicable; no CODEMANIFEST governs these three cells.\n6. **Will existing tests break?** NO — grepped all existing tests referencing WS `close`/`terminate` (`packages/platform-socket.io/test/io-adapter.spec.ts`, `integration/websockets/e2e/*.spec.ts`); none assert on `terminate` call counts, close codes, or the absence of pre-close frames, and in every e2e case the test's own client already calls `ws.close()`/is disconnected before `app.close()` runs, so `server.clients`/namespace sockets are empty by the time the new code executes in those tests.\n\n**No breaking change detected.** Pipeline may proceed to Planning.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"8eab33ad-e12f-4d41-9717-aad839a92eeb","total_cost_usd":2.2899753,"usage":{"input_tokens":87,"cache_creation_input_tokens":119880,"cache_read_input_tokens":3802731,"output_tokens":28641,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":119880,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":87,"outputTokens":28641,"cacheReadInputTokens":3802731,"cacheCreationInputTokens":119880,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.2899753,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"046295b7-ddbe-499c-b8fc-501908d4680a"}
